--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -8,0 +9,4 @@ Repo: https://github.com/openclaw/acpx
+### Changes
+
+- Sessions: add `--session-meta <json-or-file>`, a vendor-neutral session metadata option that deep-merges a JSON object over generated `_meta` on `session/new`, `session/load`, and `session/resume` across one-shot and persistent sessions. Explicit values win per leaf; arrays and scalars replace, objects merge recursively.
+
diff --git a/docs/CLI.md b/docs/CLI.md
index bd822a6..bd255ad 100644
--- a/docs/CLI.md
+++ b/docs/CLI.md
@@ -49,0 +50,8 @@ For a persistent session, close the existing session before switching its MCP co
+The global `--session-meta <json-or-file>` option attaches caller-defined metadata to the `_meta`
+field of `session/new`, `session/load`, and `session/resume` requests. The value must be a JSON
+object: inline when it starts with `{`, otherwise a file path resolved from `--cwd`. Explicit keys
+deep-merge over the `_meta` acpx generates — plain objects merge recursively while arrays and
+scalars replace — so callers can pin agent-specific namespaces such as `claudeCode.options` or any
+vendor-specific profile without dedicated flags. The metadata is persisted with the session record
+and re-applied on reconnect.
+
